Fixed the GC integration finding in 72e14cbc8a641c03d3e839e2edd711ddc3487c6c. Explicit retry now runs the maintenance owner before cleanup classification/removal, so repository backoff cannot suppress recovery. Ordinary GC retains its network-free post-cleanup pass.

The existing public-GC regression now omits manual hydration: one retry restores the missing objects and removes both eligible worktrees. It fails before the ordering fix and passes afterward. The final five-file GC run passed 55 tests with 2 skipped on the authorized Linux rig; core/services type graphs and scoped static checks passed. The PR body records the full proof and remaining historical-writer gap.

